+    SMALLEST at any scale. A tier below the box it is drawn into is not a
+    cheaper portrait, it is a blurrier one.
+
+    Used by BOTH the publish selection and `prune_orphans`, so the files already
+    on disk are removed by the same rule that stops new ones appearing. A policy
+    that only stopped publishing would leave the 14.2 MB in place forever,
+    because a reduced-tier portrait's source counterpart still exists at full
